; Stage 15 W4b sibling sweep (design/stage15-stress-test/diagnostics.md
; §W4b): found while probing `defvar` for the same class of bug. `defvar`
; legitimately requires a type annotation (unlike its siblings above), so
; `(defvar x 3)` -- no annotation at all -- is the plausible mistake here.
; The diagnostic already existed and was correctly worded, but reported line
; 0: `name-node` is a bare NODE-SYM (an interned symbol with no per-
; occurrence line), and emit-defvar read `(name-node line)` directly instead
; of borrowing the enclosing form's line via `node-line`.
(defvar x 3)

(defn main ():i32 (return x))
